  "title": "Accusative: The Usual Object",
  "updatedDate": 0,
  "fileformat": 8,
  "description": "Most verbs with a single object take the accusative; learn the forms and important constructions.",
  "intro": "For a verb with one object, the accusative is the usual case. This is a practical default, not an infallible rule: learn each verb together with its case. Accusative pronouns include mich, dich, ihn, sie, es, uns, euch, sie, Sie.",
  "sections": [
